<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tanoa Visawaqa</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1852</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tanoa Visawaqa was the Vunivalu, or war king, of Bau in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fiji">Fiji</a> from the late 1820s until his death in 1852. Driven into exile by a revolt in the 1830s, he was restored with the help of his son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seru-epenisa-cakobau">Seru Epenisa Cakobau</a> and extended Bau's dominance over much of eastern Fiji through war and tribute. Cakobau succeeded him.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tanoa-visawaqa.jpg" alt="Tanoa Visawaqa" width="320" height="442" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Alfred Thomas Agate · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ratu_Tanoa_Visawaqa.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
